# G061 — Flower Shop

*v2. See `flower-shop.md` for prose: cart as staging area, atomic checkout,
loyalty discount rule, inventory ledger consistency.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Weekly Flower Subscription

[weekly-subscription @today
    IN ORDER TO
        run every active subscription's weekly order
        as an atomic per-customer cart+checkout+email
        without a single failure affecting the others

    @subscriptions <- [db[active-subscriptions {day: @today}]]

    concurrent [
        for @sub in @subscriptions
            @cart <- [shop[new-cart {owner: @sub:customer-id,
                                        shipping: @sub:address:ship-cost}]]
            for @item in @sub:items
                [shop[add-to-cart {cart-id: @cart:id,
                                     sku: @item:sku, qty: @item:qty}]]
            [shop[apply-discount {cart-id: @cart:id,
                                    rule: [loyalty[discount
                                                    {customer: @sub:customer-id}]]}]]
            @order <- [shop[checkout {cart-id: @cart:id}]]
                      || -> #order-failed @sub:customer-id @resistance:reason
            [notifications[email {to: @sub:customer,
                                    receipt: [shop[receipt {order: @order}]]}]]
    ]
    join

    where
        every order status is "placed"
        and [shop[ledger-consistent]] is true
        and every email status is "sent"
        || -> #week-failed @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[shop
    new-cart          {owner, shipping?, tax-rate-bps?}
    add-to-cart       {cart-id, sku, qty}               ;; || out-of-stock
    update-quantity   {cart-id, sku, new-qty}
    apply-discount    {cart-id, rule}
    subtotal          {cart-or-order}
    total-discount    {cart-or-order}
    tax               {cart-or-order}
    total             {cart-or-order}
    checkout          {cart-id}                          ;; || inventory-conflict
    cancel-order      {order-id}                         ;; reversal
    fulfill-order     {order-id}
    receipt           {order}
    ledger-consistent
]

[loyalty
    discount          {customer}                         ;; looks up customer tier
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: checkout as atomic commission

[shop[checkout {cart-id: @cart}
    where
        all cart items are in stock at checkout time
        and the inventory ledger remains consistent after commit
        and either every operation commits or none does
        || emit resistance with specific reason (out-of-stock, inventory-drift, etc.)
]

Atomicity is a resolver obligation documented in the `where`. A
failed checkout leaves the cart untouched.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @shop <- [shop[new]]
    [shop[stock {sku: "rose-red", qty: 100, price-cents: 300}]]
    [shop[stock {sku: "rose-white", qty: 50, price-cents: 300}]]

    @cart <- [shop[new-cart {owner: "alice", shipping: 500}]]
    [shop[add-to-cart {cart-id: @cart:id, sku: "rose-red", qty: 12}]]
    [shop[add-to-cart {cart-id: @cart:id, sku: "rose-white", qty: 6}]]

    -> [shop[subtotal {cart-or-order: @cart}]]    ;; -> 5400 (18 × 300)
    -> [shop[total {cart-or-order: @cart}]]        ;; -> 5900 (+ 500 shipping)

    @order <- [shop[checkout {cart-id: @cart:id}]]
    -> @order:status                                 ;; -> "placed"
    -> [shop[ledger-consistent]]                     ;; -> true
]
